{
 "id": "IqDoublesC07",
 "slug": "iq-doubles/c07",
 "chapter": "The last morning",
 "topic": "What if your IQ doubled every day?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "Seven AM. Your alarm goes off. And you're tired. Normal tired."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "Your head is cool. Your mind is quiet. You're a hundred again."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "On your desk, there's a stack of notebooks in your own handwriting. You open the first one. You can't understand a single line. On the last page, there's one sentence you can read. \"Don't let them have this.\""
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "You look out of the window. The black car is gone."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "You go down to breakfast. Ellie is already there. She's eating her cereal with one hand. With the other, she's holding Mom's puzzle cube. Click, click, click. Solved."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "She looks up at you, puzzled."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "\"Why does everything feel so easy today?\""
  },
  {
   "beat": "p8",
   "text": "It only happens to you. That was the rule. So why is it happening to her?"
  },
  {
   "beat": "p9",
   "text": "What would you do? Keep the brain, or keep your family? Tell me in the comments."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p10",
   "text": "Is any of this real? The rarity of a two hundred IQ, the brain's hunger, the two thousand two hundred hours of Japanese and the million-dollar problems are all real. The sources are in the description."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p11",
   "text": "And Ellie? That's part two."
  }
 ],
